The representative of the European Union recalled concerns raised in previous statements in the Committee concerning these notifications.*&nbsp;In light of the ongoing reform of the standardization system in China, the EU asked China when the new consolidated standard(s) would be finalized and notified to the WTO, whether the announced consolidation would replace the previous ones (G/TBT/N/CHN/1094-1096), and whether its outcome would be a development of one new standard put in place of the previous ones. China was also asked to share information concerning the scope of consolidation: would the coverage of furniture product groups be the same as the previous standards, broader or narrower? What limits of harmful substances would be covered by the consolidation? Her delegation remained open to hold technical discussions in Brussels on issues regarding furniture standards, as proposed by China in June 2017. The EU reiterated its request that China designate the contact point for the organization of such a meeting.

