The representative of the European Union reiterated previously raised concerns regarding the amendments to the Safety Toy EAEU Technical Regulation.*&nbsp;In addition he recalled that during the last Committee meeting, Kazakhstan had stated that the meeting of the Working Group had taken place on 18 June 2018 to discuss amendments to the technical regulation regarding the introduction of psychological and pedagogical examination of toys at the EAEU level. It was explained that Working Group discussion had focussed on how to strike a balance between the interest of stakeholders in protecting children and the interest of foreign producers and exporters. The EU understood that that the Working Group also gave positive consideration to the ISO standard on age determination as an alternative.

