The representative of the United States reiterated previously raised concerns.*&nbsp;The US remained concerned that Ireland had not yet notified the amendments to the TBT Committee, thus denying Members the opportunity to submit comments. The US asked if Ireland would accept products that had been labelled for other EU markets or would producers have to relabel any product that first entered another EU member State that they subsequently wished to send to Ireland for sale.

