The representative of China remained concerned with India&#39;s amended regulation on toy imports.*&nbsp;His delegation urged India to accept the ISO standards (i.e. ISO 8124) as opposed to the acceptance of India&#39;s own standards (i.e. IS9873). China further noted that the amendment did not recognize laboratories accredited under ILAC MRA as it only accepted those laboratories authorized by the Indian Government. His delegation requested India to provide a transitional period for the process and to accept the international standards for the recognition of ILAC MRA labs.

